            "text": "```python\nimport os\n\n# Ensure single-threaded execution to prevent thread contention under 1-core CPU quota\nos.environ[\"OMP_NUM_THREADS\"] = \"1\"\nos.environ[\"OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS\"] = \"1\"\nos.environ[\"MKL_NUM_THREADS\"] = \"1\"\nos.environ[\"BLIS_NUM_THREADS\"] = \"1\"\nos.environ[\"VECLIB_MAXIMUM_THREADS\"] = \"1\"\nos.environ[\"NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS\"] = \"1\"\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    vectors = np.load(\"vectors.npy\")\n\n    # Compute squared L2 norms for each row\n    sq_norms = np.sum(vectors * vectors, axis=1)\n\n    # Compute Gram matrix using optimized BLAS SGEMM\n    # G[i, j] = x_i . x_j\n    d2 = vectors @ vectors.T\n\n    # In-place transform d2 into squared Euclidean distance matrix:\n    # ||x_i - x_j||^2 = ||x_i||^2 + ||x_j||^2 - 2 * (x_i . x_j)\n    d2 *= -2.0\n    d2 += sq_norms[:, None]\n    d2 += sq_norms[None, :]\n\n    # Clamp numerical precision artifacts and zero out diagonal\n    np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n    np.maximum(d2, 0.0, out=d2)\n\n    # Compute Euclidean distances\n    np.sqrt(d2, out=d2)\n\n    # Accumulate into float64 to avoid loss of precision\n    total = float(np.sum(d2, dtype=np.float64))\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
